AB  - Precise and early Crop Yield Prediction (CYP) is important to ensure food security. The prevailing Deep Learning (DL) schemes overlooked the Urease Activity (UA) analysis, limiting the prediction accuracy. Thus, a biochemical-aware CYP framework that integrates UA is proposed. Initially, the publicly available Crop Yield (CY) dataset is collected and pre-processed to improve the data quality. Next, the dimensionality of the data is reduced, followed by crop categorization. Further, the Area vs Chemical Analysis (ACA) and UA prediction are done using the Exponential Lorentzian-based Fuzzy (EL-Fuzzy). Meanwhile, the correlation heatmap is constructed, followed by feature extraction. Finally, the Transfer Learning-based Symexp Frobenius Gated Recurrent Units (TL-SFGRU) is utilized for CY prediction. Moreover, to ensure reliability, the model interpretation is carried out. The experimental outcomes demonstrate that the proposed model outperforms existing approaches by attaining an MSE of 0.1087, RMSE of 0.3296, and MAE of 0.1057. This confirms the incorporation of ACA for precise CYP.
