AB  - Aluminum alloys are essential materials for industrial development and national construction, and are widely used in metallurgy, machinery, and aerospace. The characteristics and types of inclusions in aluminum alloys significantly influence their performance. Developing a reliable system for the recognition and detection of microscopic inclusions in aluminum alloys presents significant challenges. In this study, we constructed an annotated dataset of aluminum alloy inclusions comprising six common types of inclusions. The dataset contains 3,260 images with a total of 69,374 bounding box annotations. We evaluate multiple advanced deep learning models for accurate multi-class detection of inclusion types and assess the performance of each model using various metrics. Experimental results show that the eleven models achieve mean average precision at 0.5 ranging from 72.6% to 90.5%. We further analyze detection accuracy for each inclusion type. Refractory materials and spinel inclusions are detected with over 90% accuracy across all models, while titanium diboride, oxide film, and nitride inclusions exceed 80% accuracy. This work improves the efficiency of microstructure characterization and offers potential for vision-based removal of inclusions, as well as broader applications of machine learning in materials science.
